import java.util.*;

public class Main {

	
	public static void main(String[] args) {
		// Write your code here
		Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
		int N = sc.nextInt();
		int flower[] = new int[N];

		for(int i = 0; i < N; i++){
			flower[i] = sc.nextInt();
		}

		Arrays.sort(flower);
		int cost = 0;
		int i = 0;

		while(i < N){
			int buyType = flower[i];
			cost++;

			int freeType = buyType + 4;

			while(i < N && flower[i] <= freeType){
				i++;
			}
		}

		
	System.out.println(cost);
	}

}



Oasis visits a Florist Shop. Shop has N flowers each being of a specific type and every flower costs 1 unit.
You are given type of each flower in an array P = [p1,p2,...,pN]. If he buys a flower of type P’ , then he will get all flowers whose type lies between P’ to P’+4 (both inclusive) for free.
You need to find and print the price Oasis has to pay to buy all flowers.


input :- [1, 2, 3, 10, 17]

After sorting: [1, 2, 3, 10, 17]

i = 0, buy 1 → covers 1 to 5 → skip 1,2,3
cost = 1

i = 3, buy 10 → covers 10 to 14 → skip 10
cost = 2

i = 4, buy 17 → covers 17 to 21 → skip 17
cost = 3


T.C => O(N)
S.C => O(N)
